[E0340] Error: `Ring` is indexed by a position twice
    ╭─[ err/183_indexing_by_position/main.wip:9:8 ]
    │
  9 │ extend Ring: Sequence<i64> {
    │        ──┬─
    │          ╰─── `Sequence` says what `x[i]` finds
    │
 14 │ extend Ring: Index<i64, i64> {
    │        ──┬─
    │          ╰─── and so does `Index<i64, …>`
    │
    │ Help: keep `Sequence`, which gives `x[i]` and `for` both, and remove the `Index`
    │
    │ Note: a container indexed by a position from 0 implements `Sequence`; `Index` is for a lookup whose key is not a position
────╯
[E0304] Error: `Squares::at` lends for reading
    ╭─[ err/183_indexing_by_position/main.wip:28:5 ]
    │
 28 │     table["one"] = 2
    │     ──────┬─────
    │           ╰─────── cannot be written through
    │
    │ Help: declare `var fn at(key: str): &var i64` beside it
    │
    │ Note: one name is the accessor that reads and the one that writes, and where the call sits says which
────╯
